# Rust build artifacts
/target
/target-tests

# cargo-fuzz build output + crash artifacts (seed corpora ARE committed)
/fuzz/target
/fuzz/artifacts
/fuzz/coverage
/fuzz/Cargo.lock

# Backup files from rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor / IDE
*.swp
.idea/

# Agent / tooling local overrides (committed files are the shared defaults)
.claude/agents
.claude/commands
.claude/settings.local.json
.mcp.local.json

# Design notes under docs/ stay on this machine and are never tracked: a
# glossary, setup notes and research notes that a fresh clone does not need.
# The one exception is the human guide under docs/guide/, which IS tracked —
# it is the written explanation of how the toolchain works and it ships with
# the code, so it is reviewed like any other source file.
/docs/*
!/docs/guide/

# Local run state written by the hooks (per-session injection markers): a
# decision this machine made, never a fact other checkouts should inherit.
/.rift/state/

# Machine-local integration state: capture descriptors and install manifests
# embed this machine's absolute rift binary path, and their ownership hashes
# live in the gitignored /.rift/state/ manifest — a tracked descriptor without
# its manifest reads as a conflict on every fresh clone. Never track these;
# `rift enable` regenerates them per machine.
/.rift/agents/
/.codex/hooks.json

# Local read-side caches (regenerable from the checkpoint branch / Turso projection)
**/*.duckdb
**/*.sqlite
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
/.cache

# NOTE: Cargo.lock is intentionally committed (this workspace produces a binary).

# insta pending snapshots (accepted goldens are tracked; pendings are review artifacts)
*.snap.new

# Deleted, and must stay deleted. These paths held code that was removed
# outright — the wrapper backend went in one atomic change: crate, workspace
# member, pin machinery and every product mention — and this machine's iCloud
# sync RESURRECTS deleted files: they were observed untracked-present in a
# sibling checkout on 2026-08-18. An ignore rule only works if it names the
# file exactly, so these paths are spelled in full; two FURTHER removed paths
# carrying the retired product name are deliberately absent from this list, and
# `xtask ci-meta` builds those two from fragments so that no source file ever
# stores their joined spelling.
/xtask/src/pin_cut.rs
/.rift/rewrite.toml
# The next two joined by owner decision on 2026-08-20, and they are why this
# list is not specific to the wrapper: both had been deleted once, and both came
# back as manifest-only scaffolds with an empty `src/` — STAGED, not merely
# present. No compile references them, so nothing else would have objected;
# committing them would have reddened `xtask::check_members_match_dirs`
# (a filesystem walk) in CI, on every checkout at once.
/crates/rift-fff/
/crates/rift-codegraph/
# Deleted 2026-08-25, when the recall stdio transport was retired. These two
# paths are spelled out on purpose — the entries exist to keep the deleted
# files dead, so they must name them exactly.
/.mcp.json
/bins/rift-memd/src/mcp_serve.rs
/bins/rift-doc/

data/
windsup/